menu "CH9329 BLE HID bridge"

    config BRIDGE_UART_PORT_NUM
        int "UART port for the CH9329 protocol"
        range 0 2
        default 0
        help
            UART0 is wired to the DevKit's USB-UART bridge chip (the port marked "UART"/"COM").
            The console is moved to the USB Serial/JTAG port (sdkconfig.defaults), so UART0
            carries nothing but protocol frames after boot.

    config BRIDGE_UART_TX_GPIO
        int "UART TX GPIO"
        range 0 48
        default 43

    config BRIDGE_UART_RX_GPIO
        int "UART RX GPIO"
        range 0 48
        default 44

    config BRIDGE_NOTIFY_WAIT_MS
        int "Max wait for BLE notification buffers (ms)"
        range 0 400
        default 100
        help
            When the BLE stack has no free buffer for a HID report, the bridge task waits up to
            this long (retrying every 1 ms) before answering the command with E6. It never
            answers 00 for a report that was not queued. Must stay well below the host's 500 ms
            reply timeout.

    config BRIDGE_CONN_ITVL_MIN
        int "Requested connection interval min (units of 1.25 ms)"
        range 6 3200
        default 12
        help
            12 = 15 ms. Apple Accessory Design Guidelines (section "Connection Parameters"):
            Interval Min >= 15 ms and a multiple of 15 ms; either Interval Max >= Interval Min
            + 15 ms, or both 15 ms. For BLE HID accessories "a connection interval down to
            11.25 ms (9) may be accepted by some devices". A request outside the rules may be
            rejected; the connection then keeps the iPhone's own parameters.

    config BRIDGE_CONN_ITVL_MAX
        int "Requested connection interval max (units of 1.25 ms)"
        range 6 3200
        default 12

    config BRIDGE_CONN_LATENCY
        int "Requested peripheral latency (connection events)"
        range 0 30
        default 0
        help
            0: the bridge is USB-powered and should answer LED writes promptly.

    config BRIDGE_CONN_SUPERVISION_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "Requested supervision timeout (ms)"
        range 100 32000
        default 6000
        help
            The current Apple guideline asks for 6 s to 18 s (older editions: 2 s to 6 s). This
            is how long a silently vanished phone still counts as connected: see README
            "Reliability". Shorter values may be rejected by iOS.

    config BRIDGE_ABS_MOUSE_REJECT
        bool "Answer SEND_MS_ABS_DATA with E5 instead of accepting and ignoring it"
        default n
        help
            iOS only moves its pointer for relative mice, so the bridge has no absolute pointer
            report. By default it answers 00 and drops the command (like a CH9329 whose USB host
            ignores the absolute mouse); enable this to make the host see an error instead.

    config BRIDGE_PAIR_BUTTON_GPIO
        int "Button that clears all bonds when held 3 s (-1 = none)"
        range -1 48
        default 0
        help
            GPIO0 is the DevKit's BOOT button. Holding it for 3 s after boot deletes every stored
            bond (both key sets, as Apple's guidelines require), then the bridge waits for a new
            pairing. Remove the bridge from the iPhone too (Settings > Bluetooth > (i) > Forget).

    config BRIDGE_DEVICE_NAME_PREFIX
        string "BLE name prefix when no product string is set"
        default "HID Bridge"
        help
            The advertised name is "<prefix> XXXX" (last two bytes of the Bluetooth address),
            unless SET_USB_STRING stored a product string, which then becomes the name.

endmenu
